.TH CONFIGSYS 1 "" "configsys" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
configsys \- Provision OS-native software from a profile: one config, one tool, across apt/dnf/pacman/zypper/apk/brew, plus flatpak, tarballs, language toolchains, and more
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B configsys
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIcommand\fR] [\fIargs\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provision OS-native software from a profile: one config, one tool, across apt/dnf/pacman/zypper/apk/brew, plus flatpak, tarballs, language toolchains, and more. With no command, the interactive TUI opens.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB--pretend\fR
print commands instead of executing them (dry run)
.TP
\fB--os\fR
override detected OS routes block (e.g. pop_os!)
.TP
\fB--home\fR
override HOME base for all paths (sandboxing)
.TP
\fB--config\fR
override the per-machine selector file path
.TP
\fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR
stream load detail to stderr: -v layers/overrides/per-unit state, -vv full route/binding/why (errors + progress already show by default)
.TP
\fB-q\fR, \fB--silent\fR
no console output during load at all — only the TUI ! page
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinspect\fR
show install state of the active profiles
.TP
\fBinstall\fR
Install components. A name is a component; profile:<name> expands to that profile's components.
.TP
\fBremove\fR
Uninstall components. A name is a component; profile:<name> expands to that profile's components.
.TP
\fBupgrade\fR
Upgrade components to latest. A name is a component; profile:<name> expands to that profile's components.
.TP
\fBlock\fR
Version-lock components. A name is a component; profile:<name> expands to that profile's components.
.TP
\fBunlock\fR
Remove version lock. A name is a component; profile:<name> expands to that profile's components.
.TP
\fBfix-scope\fR
reconcile installed units whose actual scope differs from the declared scope (moves the install, not config)
.TP
\fBset-version\fR
pin a component to a specific version
.TP
\fBwhere\fR
explain a component: source layer, bindings, and how it resolves on this machine
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
lint the merged config (repo + ~/configsys.hu) without installing
.TP
\fBplugin\fR
manage plugins: declare/sync, bless or init a personal primary plugin, trust code plugins
.RS
.PP
Subcommands: \fBlist\fR, \fBsync\fR, \fBbless\fR, \fBunbless\fR, \fBadd\fR, \fBremove\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBtrust\fR, \fBuntrust\fR, \fBinit\fR, \fBset-source\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fBreport\fR
assemble an install-failure report (OS + route + driver output) and file it upstream — you approve the full text first
.TP
\fBrequest\fR
ask upstream for a full cross-platform story for a component — shows a coverage matrix; you approve before filing
.TP
\fBdotfiles\fR
inspect (status) and adopt (capture) your dotfiles
.RS
.PP
Subcommands: \fBstatus\fR, \fBcapture\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fBmanpages\fR
install or check the man pages (configsys(1) + configsys.hu(5))
.RS
.PP
Subcommands: \fBinstall\fR, \fBstatus\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fBrefresh\fR
re-query latest versions from their sources
.TP
\fBshow\fR
print a shipped base data file (routes/config) or its path
.TP
\fBtui\fR
interactive TUI (default)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
  configsys                          open the interactive TUI (the default)
  configsys inspect                  install-state table for the active profiles
  configsys install rust ripgrep     install components (deps pulled + ordered)
  configsys install profile:dev       install every component in the `dev` profile
  configsys upgrade profile:dev btop  a profile plus an extra, to latest
  configsys where neovim             explain how a component resolves on this machine
  configsys show routes              print the shipped base routes.hu (or --path for its location)
  configsys --pretend install steam  dry run: print the commands, change nothing
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.nf
  CONFIGSYS_OS, CONFIGSYS_OS_VERSION   override the detected OS block / version
  CONFIGSYS_HOME, CONFIGSYS_CONFIG     relocate the HOME base / the selector file
  CONFIGSYS_NO_DISCOVER=1              disable project (.configsys.hu) discovery
  CONFIGSYS_CWD                        directory to start project discovery from
  CONFIGSYS_ARCH                       override CPU arch for $ARCH substitution
  CONFIGSYS_GITHUB_TOKEN / _GIT_TOKEN  auth for private plugin repos
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/configsys/configsys.hu\fR
per-machine config (profiles, pins, plugins).
.TP
\fB~/.config/configsys/dotfiles/\fR
machine-local dotfiles content store (see dotfiles capture).
.TP
\fB~/.config/configsys/plugins/\fR
synced plugin repos (one dir per plugin).
.TP
\fB~/.config/configsys/plugin-trust.hu\fR
approved content hashes for code plugins.
.TP
\fB~/.config/configsys/state.hu\fR
ledger: version-lock intent + bookkeeping.
.TP
\fB~/.config/configsys/versions.hu\fR
discovered-version cache (24h TTL).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR configsys.hu (5)
